completion.summary:
Boot reconstruction of a begin-unknown replay after a TermAl restart. A boot pass reads saved heads before boot recovery:
- a Prepared begin with nothing marking it possibly begun (a crash after preparation, even beside an ordinary retry) is read as begin unknown;
- begin-unknown heads get the exact begin replay;
- pre-fix heads (a retained evaluate plus an uncertain grant) get a reconstruction that replays the exact retained evaluate and begins again only the uncertain grant Engram returns, under the derived key;
- another grant, a refusal or a Defer holds the head without fabricating a begin;
- recovery runs only under the retained evaluate's authority;
- cold restore and bind leave these heads to that recovery, while a durably begun head keeps the conservative cold checkpoint and hold.
Witnesses cover new-format and pre-fix applied/expired, another grant, refused, deferred, and crash after preparation, with order assertions. Landed as a1f54018 (fast-forward on c6d6b04e), gate test-24069fe5 passed, the independent evaluation 886f0888 passed 6/6. Install is batched with w-ad17 into the next coordinator-chosen restart window.
